From 227c542cf6e648e8d7a1e32906eeb278a4296485 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 367/488] soh: name the 26 address-named symbols defined in
 z_boss_ganon2_data.c

SoH carries the Ocarina of Time decomp, in which several thousand symbols are
still named after their ROM address. This commit names every such symbol DEFINED
IN ONE FILE, so the work can be reviewed a file at a time.

The file names the unit; it does not bound it. Each rename is applied wherever
the symbol occurs -- the declaration in the header, the definition, and every
call site -- so this commit reaches into whatever other files use these symbols
and leaves no dangling reference. It is a pure rename: no behaviour changes, and
the only edits that are not renames are the provenance comments described below.

Two name sources are used, and every name says which it came from:

  * zeldaret/oot -- SoH's decomp IS zeldaret/oot at the same ROM addresses, so
    where oot has already named a symbol, that name is adopted verbatim. The
    definition gets a "Name from zeldaret/oot" comment and every declaration a
    short "// was <addr> [oot]" tag.

  * DEDUCED -- oot leaves a great many symbols address-named too, so those
    names are inferred from the body and its callers, and are marked as OURS
    rather than passed off as upstream. The definition gets
    "LLM generated name (HIGH|GUESS), was <addr>: <reason>" and the short tag
    reads "[LLM:HIGH]" or "[LLM:GUESS]". A GUESS is tagged at every call site
    as well, not only the declaration, so a reader who meets the name anywhere
    knows it is inferred. "git grep '[LLM:'" lists every place the decomp
    leans on an inference.

The justification recorded for each individual name follows, one entry per
symbol, in the order the renames were made. Nothing is summarised away: these
are the per-commit reasons from the unsquashed history, with the boilerplate
that was identical in every one of them hoisted into the text above.

All 26 are defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Boss_Ganon2/z_boss_ganon2_data.c; updating their references touches 2 files in total.

  * D_80906D60 -> sOrigin
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the zero vector pushed through the current
    matrix to read a limb's world position back out

  * D_80906D6C -> sStoneBoundSfxPos
    deduced, confidence HIGH: its only use is the position argument of the
    two NA_SE_EV_STONE_BOUND calls

  * D_80906D78 -> sSpawnRubbleRequested
    deduced, confidence HIGH: set at cutscene frame 30 alongside the rumble,
    and consumed by the next update to scatter the rubble effects

  * D_8090702C -> sSubCamEyeOffsets
    deduced, confidence HIGH: per-step eye offsets added to the player's
    position when placing the sub-camera

  * D_80907050 -> sSubCamAtOffsets
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the matching at offsets for the same
    sub-camera steps

  * D_80907074 -> sBlinkEyeIndices
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the 0-1-2-2-1-0 eye texture ramp walked by the
    blink counter

  * D_80907080 -> sSwordTrailAlpha
    deduced, confidence HIGH: prim alpha of gGanonSwordTrailDL, snapped to
    0xFF while the sword swings and stepped down by 40 afterwards

  * D_80907084 -> sSwordTrailTipVtx
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the eleven gGanonSwordTrailVtx indices fed
    from the recorded sword-tip trail

  * D_80907090 -> sSwordTrailBaseVtx
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the eleven gGanonSwordTrailVtx indices fed
    from the recorded sword-base trail

  * D_8090709C -> sLimbTrailIndices
    deduced, confidence GUESS: per-limb index handed to func_808FD080 with
    unk_424; that function's role is not established, so the trail reading
    is inferred from its pairing with the sword trail

  * D_809070CC -> sLimbPosIndices
    deduced, confidence HIGH: per-limb slot in unk_234[] where the first
    skeleton records that limb's world position

  * D_809070FC -> sSwordTrailAnchorOffset
    deduced, confidence GUESS: the hand-space point recorded as the sword
    trail's anchor at limbs 7 and 13; named for the trail it feeds, not from
    an identified model feature

  * D_80907108 -> sLimb3TrackOffset
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the offset whose transformed position limb 3
    records

  * D_80907114 -> sLimb9TrackOffset
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the offset whose transformed position limb 9
    records

  * D_80907120 -> sSwordTipOffset
    deduced, confidence HIGH: 17000 units out along the blade, the far end
    of the sword trail ribbon

  * D_8090712C -> sSwordBaseOffset
    deduced, confidence HIGH: 3000 units out along the blade, the near end
    of the same ribbon

  * D_80907138 -> sLimb45TrackOffset
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the offset whose transformed position limb 45
    records

  * D_80907144 -> sLimbPosIndices2
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the second skeleton's per-limb slot in
    unk_234[]

  * D_80907164 -> sHeadTrackOffset
    deduced, confidence GUESS: the offset limb 10 of the second skeleton
    records into the same field limb 15 fills from the origin in the first;
    the limb is head-adjacent but not confirmed

  * D_8090717C -> sBeamAnchorOffset
    deduced, confidence GUESS: passed to func_808FD080 for both hands and
    copied into unk_218; named for the effect it anchors rather than an
    identified point

  * D_80907188 -> sShadowStripeWidths6
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the six row half-widths of the narrowest limb
    stripe stamped into the shadow texture

  * D_80907194 -> sShadowStripeWidths7
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the seven row half-widths of the next limb
    stripe

  * D_809071A4 -> sShadowStripeWidths8
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the eight row half-widths of the next limb
    stripe

  * D_809071B4 -> sShadowStripeWidths12
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the twelve row half-widths of the widest limb
    stripe

  * D_809071CC -> sShadowLimbParents
    deduced, confidence HIGH: per-limb index of the limb its shadow position
    is interpolated toward, -1 where there is none

  * D_809071EC -> sShadowStripeKinds
    deduced, confidence HIGH: per-limb selector, 0-3, choosing which of the
    four stripe width tables stamps that limb

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
